ons were killed. Horst Faas, two-times Pullitzer Prize winner and Chief Photographer for The Associated Press in Saigon at the height of the war, and Tim Page, another veteran who had been badly wounded, have gathered many thousands of photos from the Western agencies and from archives in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City. These have now been assembled to form both a monument to the dead and a record of the most terrifying war photography ever taken. Never again will the media have the kind of access to the war zone that was offered to the photographers in Vietnam. In many cases the photographers tried to get as close as possible, then paid the price.","pageCount":348,"publicationYear":1997,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"History","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-requiem-horst-faas-and-tim-page"}],"displaySummary":"In many cases the photographers tried to get as close as possible, then paid the price.","primarySubject":"History","primaryTopic":"Vietnam War","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"History","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"History","score":3,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"History","mappedSubject":"History","score":3,"confidence":"medium","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-requiem-horst-faas-and-tim-page","id":"subject-evidence-book-requiem-horst-faas-and-tim-page-1"},{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"Society & Culture","mappedSubject":"Society & Culture","score":2,"confidence":"low","note":"war/military keyword; society/culture keyword","id":"subject-evidence-book-requiem-horst-faas-and-tim-page-3"},{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"War & Military","mappedSubject":"War & Military","score":2,"confidence":"low","note":"war/military keyword; society/culture keyword","id":"subject-evidence-book-requiem-horst-faas-and-tim-page-2"},{"source":"topic_classifier","rawLabel":"